// How the academy worker gets deployed from a clone of this repo.
//
// This is not a build step and the game does not know it exists. It is a
// description of where worker.js goes and what it needs bound to it, so
// that `wrangler deploy` in this folder is the whole of a release rather
// than a series of clicks in a dashboard that have to be remembered.
//
// On a new machine, once:
//
//     npx wrangler login                       (approve in the browser)
//     npx wrangler kv namespace create ACADEMY (prints the id below)
//     npx wrangler deploy
//     npx wrangler secret put DIRECTOR_PASSWORD
//
// The id below is not a secret. It names a namespace inside one
// Cloudflare account and is useless to anybody who cannot authenticate
// as that account, which is why it can sit in a public repository when
// an API key never could. The password is the opposite, and is why the
// last line of that list is a separate command you type yourself: it is
// set on the worker and stored by Cloudflare, and it appears nowhere in
// this repository, in this file, or in the game.
{
  "name": "academy",
  "main": "worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-12",
  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "ACADEMY",
      "id": "13c699bcf35f4356926a47f84912098e"
    }
  ]
}
